title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and marcher_toleration and not marcher_toleration_right and chancellor_party == "Unionist" and not concord_formed
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, we can still provide support.

= Dealing with Toleration

We are currently acting as external support to the government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +]. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_against_austerity
- @urge_against_austerity_limited
- @urge_paramilitary
- @improve_relations
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
view-if: not constructive_vonc
title: End the toleration agreement with a vote of no confidence!

Are we sure about this? A vote of no confidence would trigger new elections, and potentially an increased vote-share for the extremist parties. [? if in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] also threatens a no-confidence vote against us in Heartland, pressuring us to stay the course.?]

- @vonc: Yes, end this arrangement!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@vonc
on-arrival: marcher_in_government = 0; marcher_toleration = 0; marcher_toleration_right = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Askew"; chancellor_party = "Unionist"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; left_strength += 8; pro_republic -= 5; burgher_marcher -= 3; landed_marcher -= 3; guild_marcher -= 3; faithful_marcher -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 5; gold_relation -= 4; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; ddp_right += 1; gold_right += 2; marcher_break_toleration += 1
go-to: new_prussia_election if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and ((center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"); center_right_coalition_prussia if in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland or in_weimar_coalition_heartland or in_grand_coalition_heartland or in_popular_front_heartland and (((center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 or right_coalition_heartland >= 50) and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate") or bourgeois_coalition_heartland >= 50)

We have called for a vote of no confidence, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@new_prussia_election
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; collectivist_relation += 5; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; lvp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; burgher_marcher -= 2; landed_marcher -= 2; guild_marcher -= 2; faithful_marcher -= 2; burgher_royalist += 2; guild_royalist += 2; landed_royalist += 2; faithful_royalist += 2; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_social_catholic_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory vote in Heartland, forcing the dissolution of the state Assembly for new elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland +].

A double dissolution has shaken the people's faith in democracy, with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader.

@center_right_coalition_prussia
on-arrival: in_center_right_coalition_heartland = 1; in_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; in_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_grand_coalition_heartland = 0; in_popular_front_heartland = 0; in_left_front_heartland = 0; in_marcher_majority_heartland = 0; in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 0; in_minority_weimar_coalition_heartland = 0; marcher_heartland = 0; right_heartland = 0; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 0; collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 0; marcher_toleration_heartland = 0; heartland_coalition_trigger = 0; heartland_leader = "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; burgher_marcher -= 3; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; pro_republic -= 3; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.06; heartland_police_strength -= 8; 

The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has called a retaliatory no confidence vote in Heartland, replacing our government with a center-right coalition composed of all parties to our right, except for the <span style="color: #003755;">**DNF**</span> and <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>. While this is a setback, it is not the worst possible outcome, as new elections could have led to significant gains for extremist parties.

[? if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick": Adam Sedgewick?][? if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick": Heinrich Askew?] of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland.

@urge_against_austerity
title: Urge the coalition against austerity politics, and to increase social spending.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: This can only happen with a budget surplus.
go-to: urge_success if unionist_relation >= 45 and ((ddp_relation >= 40 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation >= 40 and lvp_formed)); urge_failure if unionist_relation < 45 or ((ddp_relation < 40 and not lvp_formed) or (lvp_relation < 40 and lvp_formed))

@urge_success
on-arrival: welfare += 1; budget -= 1; commons_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 5*(1-dissent); burgher_ddp += 1; guild_ddp += 1; burgher_gold += 1.5; guild_gold += 1.5; burgher_other += 1.5; guild_other += 1.5; burgher_lvp += 3; guild_lvp += 3; unionist_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5; gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 0.5; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry_bruning += 10; economic_growth += 0.2; disfavored -= 0.2

We have successfully urged the coalition parties to increase social spending! Unfortunately, the center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations. [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour is also losing patience with Askew for yielding to our demands.?]

@urge_failure
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 3; gold_relation -= 3; ddp_relation -= 3; lvp_relation -= 3

Unfortunately, our negotiations have met with failure. The center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations.

@urge_against_austerity_limited
title: Attempt to pressure Askew to curb the worse excesses of his austerity policies. 
go-to: urge_success_limited if unionist_relation >= 35; urge_failure if unionist_relation < 35

@urge_success_limited
on-arrival: bruning_austerity_limited += 1; commons_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 3*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 3*(1-dissent) if bruning_austerity_limited >= 3; burgher_ddp += 1; guild_ddp += 1; burgher_gold += 1; guild_gold += 1; burgher_other += 1; guild_other += 1; burgher_royalist -= 2; guild_royalist -= 2; burgher_lvp += 2; guild_lvp += 2; unionist_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 3; center_dissent -= 3; labor_dissent -= 3; gold_right += 1; ddp_right += 0.5; lvp_right += 1; dufour_angry_bruning += 5; economic_growth += 0.1; disfavored -= 0.1

We have successfully pressured Askew to tone down the severity of his austerity policies in his emergency decrees. Unfortunately, the center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and will attempt to force Askew to form a majority coalition with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span>-<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> instead. [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour is also losing patience with Askew for yielding to our demands.?]

[? if bruning_austerity_limited == 1: We have successfully prevented Askew from decreasing taxes on high earners, lessening the burden of compensatory tax increases on the lower strata. ?][? if bruning_austerity_limited == 2: We have successfully pressured Askew into attempting to appease us by reinstating the 40-hour workweek, however wages themselves remains suboptimal. ?][? if bruning_austerity_limited >= 3: We have successfully pressured Askew in reversing some salary cuts to civil servants. ?]

@urge_paramilitary
view-if: political_decree < 2 and not loyalist_nationwide_ban
choose-if: marcher_heartland and strife >= 3 and unionist_relation >= 35 and not second_bruning_cabinet_seen
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not marcher_heartland: We don't control the Heartland government. ?] [? if strife < 3: Paramilitary violence isn't severe enough to justify an emergency decree. ?] [? if unionist_relation < 35: We lack sufficient relations with Askew. ?] [? if second_bruning_cabinet_seen: Joseph Werth is no longer in charge of the Interior Ministry, meaning we can no longer rely on his connections. ?]
title: Urge Askew to grant us stronger actions against political extremists, and to restrict certain rights.
on-arrival: political_decree += 1; heartland_police_loyalty += 0.04; heartland_police_strength += 5; collectivist_relation -= 6; vanguard_militancy *= 0.9; vanguard_strength *= 0.85; loyalist_militancy *= 0.96; loyalist_strength *= 0.96; warden_militancy *= 0.98; warden_strength *= 0.98; commons_collectivist -= 1; commons_royalist -= 1; disfavored_collectivist -= 3; disfavored_royalist -= 3; burgher_royalist -= 2; dufour_angry_bruning += 5

Carl Heath and other Heartland officials have successfully urged Askew to issue an emergency decree expanding police authority to suppress political extremism. The decree imposes restrictions on political meetings, organizations, newspapers, and posters, all of which now require police approval beforehand.

As a result, several <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalist</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">Communist</span> newspapers have been banned, triggering violent clashes between their supporters and the police. [? if president == "DuFour": President DuFour has reluctantly signed the decree, but is losing patience with Askew for yielding to our demands. ?]

@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with the parties of the coalition.
on-arrival: unionist_relation += 5*(1-dissent); gold_relation += 4*(1-dissent); ddp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); lvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 5; gold_left += 1; ddp_left += 0.5; ddp_cohesion -= 0.5; lvp_left += 1

We have increased our level of contact and discussions with the parties of the coalition, primarily the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] [? if not lvp_formed and gold_exist:and <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if lvp_formed:and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**LVP**</span>?].

Our attempts to reach out to the center-right are met with disdain by leftists within our party.

@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
